Inclusion Criteria:

1. Healthy adults aged 19-65 years, inclusive, with no active respiratory or other medical conditions that may affect study outcomes;
2. no use of tobacco, vaping devices, or cannabis within the previous 6 months and a lifetime smoking history of less than 0.5 pack-years;
3. no known hypersensitivity or allergy to Advil (ibuprofen); and
4. female participants must be postmenopausal, surgically sterile, or using medically accepted contraception, and must not be pregnant or nursing during the study.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Body mass index (BMI) ≥35 kg/m²;
2. unable to withhold antihistamines, leukotriene antagonists, immunotherapy, or corticosteroid medications for the duration of the study;
3. active medical conditions that may affect respiratory or inflammatory outcomes or increase risk during controlled wood smoke exposure, including asthma, allergic rhinitis, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), active infections, diabetes, long COVID, tuberculosis, or heart conditions;
4. planned hospitalization(s) or blood donation during the study period; and (e) high background exposure to air pollution or dust through residence, leisure activities, or occupation;
5. Are taking other NSAIDs at the time of the active portion of the study;
6. high background exposure to air pollution or dust through residence, leisure activities, or occupation; and
7. current participation in another research study involving a study drug or controlled exposure, or participation in one within 4-weeks before screening.
